  "source": "The Public Health Agency of Sweden",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: Percentage (%) of the population (16–84 years or 16 years and older) that has used narcotic drugs for medical use other than as prescribed during the past 30 days or during the past 12 months. Response rate for the Swedish National Public Health Survey: 2018 (42,1 %), 2020 (42,3 %), 2021 (44,1 %), 2022 (37,9 %), 2024 (39,4 %). The survey is conducted every two years. In 2021, an extra round of the survey was conducted due to the ongoing corona pandemic."
